Revision history for unreagent

{{$NEXT}}
  - ${ENGINE} is detected from the EngineAssociation in the .uproject:
    Launcher versions and source-build ids resolve, every registered Launcher
    install counts, and versions compare numerically (5.10 beats 5.9).
  - Permission layer: Bash rules match per shell segment (chains, grouping,
    substitution, nested shells); deny fires on any segment, allow only when
    every segment is covered. Deny sees through quoting and sudo/env/eval.
  - Non-Bash rules such as Read(...) or WebFetch(...) match the tool's path,
    pattern, url or query input, with normalised paths; a rule without an
    evaluable input fails closed.
  - The permission layer is enforced in headless mode only. On Windows the
    shell tool is PowerShell, so rules are written PowerShell(...).
  - MCP server hardening: foreign Origins get 403, POSTs need Content-Type
    application/json, bodies are size-limited, timeouts are set, and a
    panicking tool (even panic(nil)) becomes a tool error.
  - JSON-RPC handling follows the spec: "id": null is a request, batches are
    validated per element, bad framing answers -32600, initialize negotiates
    protocolVersion, and the Bearer scheme is case-insensitive.
  - write_file and edit_file reject a missing content or new_string argument
    (and edit_file an empty path) instead of truncating the file or deleting
    every match; read_file declares path required.
  - run_python and run_node run scripts inside the runtime's project
    directory, so imports resolve against the project; scripts left by a hard
    kill are swept at startup.
  - status lists a service with a stuck control loop as "unresponsive" instead
    of omitting it, and queries all services concurrently.
  - Process output is no longer lost: lines over 1 MiB are split instead of
    stalling the child, and a crashing process's last lines reach the log.
    run_command keeps only the head and tail of very large outputs.
  - A failed start (e.g. agent.command not on PATH) is reported as an exit
    instead of leaving a dead console; a failing Job Object setup is logged
    and the process runs unsupervised instead of crashing the launcher.
  - The taskbar flash feature (flash_task tool, "unreagent flash" sub-command,
    Stop hook) is removed; it never worked reliably.
  - Tool descriptions, log lines and error messages are English throughout.
  - make windows stops with a clear error when the .syso resource is an
    unfetched Git LFS pointer.
  - Building needs Go 1.26 or newer (the go directive was 1.19); CI and the
    release build use Go 1.27 and run the test suite before building.
  - README documents Unreal MCP (UE 5.8+, HTTP :8000) next to the UE LLM
    Toolkit, the refreshed requirements, MCP hardening, the Git LFS build
    note and a new architecture graphic; it links the unreagent-example
    project.
  - local.yaml overlays by YAML decode, not deep merge: a list replaces the
    base list, a map merges by key with each given entry replaced whole.

0.0.8     2026-06-12 05:42:04Z
  - Hermes Agent support: "unreagent hermes-setup" sub-command and the
    agent.hermes.* settings; see the README section on Hermes Agent.
  - Optional bearer authentication on the MCP server via mcp.token.

0.0.7     2026-06-12 03:15:56Z
  - Windows taskbar flash at the end of an agent turn: flash_task MCP tool and
    "unreagent flash" sub-command, with a Stop hook attached to Claude Code
    when agent.claudeIntegration is on.
  - Windows metadata: publisher and version in the .exe resource, asInvoker
    manifest, new icon; self-signed code-signing certificate with an import
    script.
  - Agent runs in its own window by default, inherits the real console in
    interactive mode, handles /quit without hanging the launcher and does not
    restart-loop on a missing program; agent.env sets extra variables.
  - MCP bridges (initialize handshake, in-editor plugin port) are checked
    before the agent starts; MCP config can be written as .mcp.json or for
    VS Code.
  - UE crash dialog and recovery prompt are handled unattended.
  - Flags -no-agent and -files; file tools read_file, write_file, list_dir
    and edit_file over MCP.
  - First release: launcher supervising the UE editor and an agent (Job
    Objects, restart policy, ring-buffer logs), MCP server with status, logs,
    ue_start/ue_stop/ue_restart, run_command, run_python, run_node and the
    approve permission tool, YAML config with ${ENGINE}/${PROJECT}
    placeholders and a local overlay, runnable ping demo.
